### 2. Voice Context & Real-Time Conversation Loop

#### [MODIFY] [SmartAgentSessionContext.tsx](file:///d:/Institute/BCE/src/features/analytics/context/SmartAgentSessionContext.tsx)

- Refactor `SmartAgentSessionContext`:
  - Introduce explicit state enum: `IDLE`, `LISTENING`, `HEARING`, `FINALIZING`, `TRANSCRIBING`, `THINKING`, `SPEAKING_AI`, `STOPPED`.
  - Implement Web Audio VAD monitoring loop in context:
    - `LISTENING` -> `HEARING`: Triggered automatically when speech energy crosses `SPEECH_ENERGY_THRESHOLD`.
    - `HEARING` -> `FINALIZING`: Triggered automatically when silence is detected for `750ms`.
    - `FINALIZING` -> `TRANSCRIBING`: Automatically extracts speech segment blob and posts to `/api/ai/transcribe` with `sttAbortControllerRef`.
    - `TRANSCRIBING` -> `THINKING`: Posts transcript to `askSmartAgentAction` with `agentAbortControllerRef`.
    - `THINKING` -> `SPEAKING_AI`: Triggers `speakAssistantResponse`.
    - `SPEAKING_AI` -> `LISTENING`: Upon TTS completion (`onEnd`), automatically transitions back to `LISTENING`.
  - **Barge-in / AI Speech Interruption**:
    - During `SPEAKING_AI`, monitor VAD for user speech.
    - If user speech energy exceeds barge-in threshold for >250ms, immediately call `stopAssistantSpeech()`, abort pending requests, and switch to `HEARING` to capture the new command!
  - **Self-Feedback Suppression**: Suppress mic processing during AI speaker output unless user speech crosses high barge-in threshold.
  - **AbortController Management**: Maintain `sttAbortControllerRef` and `agentAbortControllerRef`. Abort pending requests when session changes, Voice is turned OFF, Stop is clicked, or drawer is closed.

